  "observations": [
    "Complete real Skreecher registerGoals installs player target and FollowTargetGoal. Its target box is horizontal16 inflated entity box and Y[-64,320]. Follow requires live own target and clingCooldown<=0; within horizontal2.5 it sets clapping. Native superclass scheduling/priority execution was not expanded.",
    "Complete native tick clap block qualifies clapping+ownalive+cooldown<=0. Every8 clap counter requests roar/gameEvent/nearby anger, with15 branch else-if; these are state/alarm cues, never new Warden proof. At clapTick>=100 and enabled config, if not already attempted, it sets hasAttemptedWardenSpawning=true BEFORE ground search, side check, local existing-Warden test and biome tag. False config leaves attempt unconsumed while clap can continue; default/assignment is not actual runtime config.",
    "The downward search stops at Y<=-64 even without a confirmed sturdy face. A true server-side block plus empty local Warden query and allowed biome requests create, moveTo, finalizeSpawn(TRIGGERED), setAttackTarget, increaseAngerAt79false and addFreshEntity. No create null guard, bounding-box/obstruction/ordinary NaturalSpawner cap check or add-result check in shown caller. Ground/biome/existing-Warden rejection still consumed attempt; no retry/reset in this complete entity.",
    "Only actual entity addition is server guarded inside trigger. Local attempted flag and ground/biome lookups are outside explicit server guard, so no cross-side attempt convergence is asserted. Server target/LOS/invisibility/blindness/horizontal20 validation occurs AFTER potential spawn attempt in tick. This proves order, not a reproduced stale-target spawn.",
    "Nearby query uses AABB with X/Z +/-35 and Y arguments ownY+(cling?5:25), -64. Actual native AABB constructor min/max normalizes both ends; reverse-written Y is not proof of empty box. It is a local current-level query, not a sphere, global unique encounter lock, reservation or guarantee against two actors producing overlapping encounters.",
    "Own NBT SummonedWarden is the attempted boolean, not successful spawn receipt. Clinging/CeilDist/ClingCooldown also serialize; clapTick and clapping do not. setClapping(false) resets clapTick but never clears attempt. Native hurt clears cling/clap and sets random200..399 cooldown BEFORE super.hurt result, so a rejected attempt may still request interruption. No successful-HP condition qualifies this cleanup.",
    "Actual SKREECHER EntityType registry uses CREATURE despite Monster superclass; its own placement requires nonpeaceful, native darkness and SCULK, plus instance roll helper (SPAWNER bypass). Warden is a different TRIGGERED direct-add source, not proof that original Dynasty NATURAL CREATURE cap opportunity opened. Fixed allowed-biome resource is nonreplacing minecraft:deep_dark; installed tags/deployment remain unobserved.",
    "Native Warden finalizeSpawn(TRIGGERED) sets DIG_COOLDOWN1200, EMERGING pose and temporary IS_EMERGING plus a sound request, then delegates superclass. setAttackTarget writes ATTACK_TARGET Brain memory and resets other memories/cooldown; increaseAngerAt separately checks noAI/canTargetEntity before anger request. Target assignment/anger/pose/sound before add are not successful entity-added acknowledgments or actual attack evidence.",
    "Native ServerLevel.addFreshEntity delegates boolean addEntity, which rejects already-removed entities or entityManager failure and only calls onAddedToWorld on successful manager add. Skreecher ignores this boolean. EntityManager admission/event/UUID internals were not expanded. Warden removeWhenFarAway false alone is not immortal/forever or full digging lifetime proof."
  ],
